{"profile":{"name":"Paula Fletcher","ward":"Ward 14, Toronto—Danforth","bio":"First elected to Toronto City Council in 2003 to represent the former Ward 30; re-elected in 2018 and 2022 to represent Ward 14 Toronto-Danforth. Before council she was elected as a Toronto District School Board trustee in 2000 and was a leader in the East End Parent Network; she has served as Deputy Speaker of City Council since August 2023 and as Chair of the Infrastructure and Environment Committee since May 2025. On August 19, 2026 she announced she will retire from politics at the end of the 2022-2026 term and will not seek re-election.","committees":["Executive Committee","Infrastructure and Environment Committee (Chair)","Audit Committee (Vice-Chair)","Corporations Nominating Panel (Chair)","Civic Appointments Committee","Service Excellence Committee","Toronto and East York Community Council","Film, Television and Digital Media Advisory Board (Chair)","CreateTO Board of Directors (Mayor's Designate)","TO Live Board of Directors (Mayor's Designate)","Toronto and Region Conservation Authority","Toronto Parking Authority","Canadian Stage Company"],"contact":{"email":"councillor_fletcher@toronto.ca","phone":"416-392-4060"},"promises":[{"text":"Signed the Toronto Environmental Alliance's Greener City for All election pledge in 2022, committing to support priority actions including fully funding Toronto's climate strategy (2025/2030/2040 targets), overhauling heating and cooling bylaws and a fair stormwater charge for climate resilience, and regulations to eliminate unnecessary single-use items toward a zero-waste city.","source":"http://election.torontoenvironment.org/pledge_results"},{"text":"Signed the Toronto Alliance to End Homelessness's Pledge to End Homelessness in 2022, committing to make ending homelessness through housing solutions a top City priority in the coming term, set minimum housing access targets for people experiencing homelessness, increase financial resources through a dedicated fund, and develop a Toronto Ending Homelessness Plan.","source":"https://paul-bruce-o84i.squarespace.com/s/THHSP-Forum-Slide-Deck-November-16-2022.pdf"}]},"lobbying":{"total":874,"term":192,"first":"2010-08-24","last":"2026-10-08","lobbyists":211,"clients":190,"subjects":421,"methods":{"Meetings":158,"Emails":487,"Phone calls":99,"Written":86,"Other or unreported":44},"top":[{"label":"Economic Development","count":179},{"label":"By-law / Regulation","count":126},{"label":"Licences / Licensing","count":111},{"label":"Affordable Housing","count":92},{"label":"Planning and Development Application, Zoning By-law","count":86}],"years":[{"year":2010,"count":2},{"year":2011,"count":24},{"year":2012,"count":34},{"year":2013,"count":60},{"year":2014,"count":53},{"year":2015,"count":60},{"year":2016,"count":73},{"year":2017,"count":58},{"year":2018,"count":29},{"year":2019,"count":57},{"year":2020,"count":57},{"year":2021,"count":65},{"year":2022,"count":57},{"year":2023,"count":62},{"year":2024,"count":53},{"year":2025,"count":49},{"year":2026,"count":19}],"undated":62,"snapshot":"2026-10-23"},"declaredInterests":[{"Declarant":"Paula Fletcher","VerbalDeclarationDate":"2021-09-09","Committee":"Toronto and East York Community Council","Item":"2021.TE27.72","ItemTitle":"Speed Hump Installation on Fairmount Crescent from Bowmore Road to Bellhaven Road","VerbalDeclaration":"as the proposed speed humps are in close proximity to my home address.","WrittenDeclaration":"https://secure.toronto.ca/council/declared-interest-file.do?id=10136","ReceiveDate":"2021-09-09","Term":"2018-2022"},{"Declarant":"Paula Fletcher","VerbalDeclarationDate":"2021-09-09","Committee":"Toronto and East York Community Council","Item":"2021.TE27.91","ItemTitle":"Speed Hump Installation on Bowmore Road from Gerrard Street East to Wrenson Road","VerbalDeclaration":"as the proposed speed humps are in close proximity to my home address.","WrittenDeclaration":"https://secure.toronto.ca/council/decla